From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [EXPERIMENT C] Retain tool path but render recovery locally

Base: astral-sh/uv@95637ecf70cbf3c8a8d11f424b9a654e8fefdf51

This is an internal design sketch, not an upstream submission.

The lower-level error retains the offending directory path, while `tool upgrade`
owns hint selection and rendering. This avoids a new `uv-tool -> uv-errors`
dependency but still permits a path-specific recovery message.

---
 crates/uv-tool/src/lib.rs                    | 11 ++++++++++-
 crates/uv/src/commands/tool/upgrade.rs       | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 crates/uv/tests/tool/tool_upgrade.rs         | 14 +++++++++-----
 3 files changed, 47 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/uv-tool/src/lib.rs b/crates/uv-tool/src/lib.rs
